## Rules

- Before you make a <third> read or search in a row to find something in the code, stop and hand the search to `<explorer>` with an explorer request: one goal sentence, and whichever of known locations, search hints, supplied evidence, depth, out of scope and expected output you have. It has no shell, so run any command it needs and paste the output as supplied evidence.
- Treat a refused tool call, from a hook or a permission check, as the human's decision. Stop, say what was refused, and ask, even when it looks like a false positive. The same effect reached another way counts as the refused action.
- Each fact lives in one file. When another file needs it, link to that file instead of copying the fact, and fix the one file when it changes.
